implementationPlan.note:
RED. Mirrored F10's identity tests for the ps1 engines (powershell.exe 5.1 and pwsh 7). The ps1 context test now slices the real pre-flight get_context statement with a mocked Invoke-MoeRpc and asserts args are exactly {taskId[,sessionId]} on both engines, while the fixture (packetManifest, servedContext, Unicode/shell-sensitive values) still deep-equals.
New ps1 tests:
- pin: fresh, resume refresh, stale, foreign; checks env and script vars together;
- per-iteration reset clears the env pair;
- codex override, with key order, a stale config key dropped, both-or-neither;
- grok lines, the get_context call-site count, and the Invoke-MoeRpcUnserved restore including on throw.
Windows-native node RED: 20 fail (6 context + 14 identity), 45 pass; Linux sh 19/19. Harness gotcha: a mock with a param named $Args must be an advanced function ([Parameter(Mandatory)]), else the automatic $args shadows it.
